sequenceDiagram
    %% ─── Participants ────────────────────────────────────────────────
    participant PD  as platformd<br/>(Server VM)
    participant CA  as CA<br/>(go-xkms via go-quicbaas SDK)
    participant DNS as DNS Service<br/>(CoreDNS + DNSSEC<br/>:8053 / :9053)
    participant DP  as DANEPublisher
    participant API as REST API<br/>(:8443)
    participant TT  as Test Tool<br/>(Host)
    participant TS  as truststrap Client<br/>(DANE Bootstrapper)
    participant CV  as Client VM<br/>(platformd)

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    rect rgb(20, 40, 70)
        Note over PD,API: ── SERVER STARTUP FLOW ──────────────────────────────────────────

        PD->>PD: platformd starts
        PD->>PD: App.Init()

        %% DNS startup
        PD->>DNS: Start DNS service (:8053 public, :9053 internal)
        activate DNS
        DNS-->>PD: DNS service running

        Note over DNS: [FIX] Zones created with EMPTY tenant IDs initially.<br/>Tenant claims happen lazily in ensureZoneTenantID() (step g).
        DNS->>DNS: Create zones: example.com. / example.internal.<br/>(tenant IDs = "" at this point)
        DNS->>DNS: DNSSEC sign zones (KSK + ZSK generated)
        DNS-->>PD: Zones ready, DNSSEC active

        %% CA initialization
        PD->>CA: Load / initialize CA
        activate CA
        CA->>CA: Initialize root CA
        CA->>CA: Initialize intermediate CA
        CA-->>PD: CA ready (root + intermediate)

        %% Web server initialization
        PD->>PD: InitWebServer()

        loop For each webservice (public :8443, internal)
            PD->>CA: issueWebServiceCertificate()
            CA->>CA: Issue TLS leaf cert signed by intermediate CA
            CA-->>PD: TLS certificate (leaf + chain)

            Note over PD,DP: publishDANETLSA() hook fires after certificate issuance

            PD->>PD: publishDANETLSA()

            Note over PD: [FIX] ServiceRegistry() lazy-inits the DNS service reference<br/>on App. Was previously nil when publishDANETLSA ran.
            PD->>DNS: ServiceRegistry() — lazy-init DNS service ref on App
            DNS-->>PD: DNS service ref resolved

            PD->>DP: DANEPublisher.PublishForCertificate(cert, caCert)
            activate DP

            DP->>DP: Compute DANE-TA (Usage=2)<br/>SPKI SHA-256 from CA cert
            DP->>DP: Compute DANE-EE (Usage=3)<br/>SPKI SHA-256 from leaf cert (if enabled)

            Note over DP,DNS: [FIX] ensureZoneTenantID() claims the zone for "platform"<br/>tenant on first TLSA write — resolves the empty tenant ID.
            DP->>DNS: AddTLSARecord()<br/>→ get zone from DAO<br/>→ ensureZoneTenantID() claims zone for "platform" tenant<br/>→ insert TLSA record
            DNS-->>DP: Record added

            DP->>DNS: SaveAndSign()<br/>DNSSEC re-signs zone with new TLSA records
            DNS-->>DP: Zone re-signed, AD flag valid
            deactivate DP

            DNS-->>PD: TLSA records published
        end

        %% REST API ready
        PD->>API: Start REST API (:8443)
        activate API
        API->>API: Register /api/v1/ca/bootstrap
        API-->>PD: REST API listening

        PD-->>PD: Server READY<br/>(ping + :8053 DNS + :8443 HTTPS all responding)
    end

    %% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    rect rgb(20, 55, 20)
        Note over TT,CV: ── CLIENT BOOTSTRAP FLOW (Test Tool → Client VM) ──────────────

        TT->>TT: waitForCSServerReady()<br/>polls ping + DNS(:8053) + HTTPS(:8443)
        TT-->>TT: Server detected as ready

        TT->>TT: fetchCSCABundle()
        TT->>TT: Resolve DNS server from config<br/>dns.resolver.servers[0] = 10.99.99.2:8053

        Note over TT: [FIX] Server hostname resolved from server config<br/>(domain = server.example.com), NOT the IP address.<br/>Prevents bogus TLSA lookup on _8443._tcp.10.99.99.2.
        TT->>TT: Resolve server hostname from server config<br/>domain = server.example.com

        TT->>TS: Create bootstrap.Client (strategy = DANE)
        activate TS

        TT->>TS: bootstrap.Client.FetchCABundle()

        TS->>TS: Create truststrap DANEBootstrapper:<br/>  ServerURL  = https://10.99.99.2:8443<br/>  Hostname   = server.example.com<br/>  DNSServer  = 10.99.99.2:8053

        Note over TS: [FIX] dane.Resolver is auto-created from the DNSServer field.<br/>Was previously nil, causing a nil-pointer panic at TLSA lookup.
        TS->>TS: Create dane.Resolver from DNSServer (10.99.99.2:8053)

        TS->>DNS: TLSA query: _8443._tcp.server.example.com. TLSA<br/>@ 10.99.99.2:8053
        DNS-->>TS: TLSA records returned (DANE-TA Usage=2,<br/>CA cert SPKI SHA-256 hash)

        TS->>TS: Verify DNSSEC AD flag (authenticated data)<br/>on TLSA response

        Note over TS,API: TLS verification uses DANE (TLSA records),<br/>NOT the system CA trust store
        TS->>API: GET https://10.99.99.2:8443/api/v1/ca/bootstrap<br/>(TLS verified via DANE / TLSA)
        API-->>TS: PEM certificate bundle (root + intermediate)

        TS->>TS: Verify CA bundle SPKI hash<br/>against retrieved TLSA records

        TS-->>TT: CA bundle verified
        deactivate TS

        TT->>TT: Write CA bundle to disk

        alt Strategy = "embedded"
            TT->>CV: Embed CA bundle in client ISO<br/>(available at first boot, no runtime fetch needed)
            CV-->>TT: Bundle embedded
        else Strategy = "dane"
            Note over CV: Client VM bootstraps at runtime:<br/>performs its own DANE lookup + CA fetch on startup
            CV->>CV: Runtime DANE bootstrap<br/>(same truststrap flow, runs on VM boot)
        end
    end

    deactivate CA
    deactivate DNS
    deactivate API
